From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:28:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nvkms: don't yield after wrapping a display push buffer

nvEvoMakeRoom() waits for space in a display channel's push buffer
(4 KiB per channel). When the space left before the end is too small and
GET isn't at the start, it writes a jump to the start, kicks off and sets
PUT to 0, which frees everything from the start up to GET. But it doesn't
recompute fifo_free_count, which still holds the space that was left
before the end, so the loop goes on to call nvkms_yield() (schedule())
before reading GET again and finding the room. That happens once per lap
of every channel's push buffer, from the flip path, with the global NVKMS
lock and the DRM modeset locks held.

On an RTX 4080 Laptop (AD104) with KWin flipping an external 160 Hz
DisplayPort monitor while a video plays, a kprobe on nvkms_yield() saw
exactly one yield per such wait, all in nvEvoMakeRoom() on the head's
window channel, about every 50 ms (every 8-9 flips). The atomic commits
that hit it took p50 197 us against 93 us for the others (p90 250 us
against 121 us): when schedule() runs another task first, the commit
thread loses about 100 us.

Check for room again right after wrapping instead. The next pass reads GET
with PUT at 0: either GET is back at 0 and the whole buffer is free, or the
space up to GET is checked as before, so it can't wrap again and only
yields if the channel really has to make progress first.

nvidia_modeset.pushbuf_wrap_no_yield=0 (module parameter, writable at
runtime) restores the old behaviour.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-linux.c    | 11 +++++++++++
 .../nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-os-interface.h     |  1 +
 .../include/nvidia-modeset-os-interface.h            |  1 +
 src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-dma.c                   | 12 ++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-linux.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-linux.c
index b65f927e..190791ad 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-linux.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-linux.c
@@ -174,6 +174,12 @@ MODULE_PARM_DESC(kapi_sysmem_semaphores,
 static bool kapi_sysmem_semaphores = true;
 module_param_named(kapi_sysmem_semaphores, kapi_sysmem_semaphores, bool, 0444);
 
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(pushbuf_wrap_no_yield,
+                 "When a display channel push buffer wraps around, check for room again right away "
+                 "instead of yielding the CPU first (with the NVKMS lock held).");
+static bool pushbuf_wrap_no_yield = true;
+module_param_named(pushbuf_wrap_no_yield, pushbuf_wrap_no_yield, bool, 0644);
+
 /* Fail allocating the RM core channel for NVKMS using the i-th method (see
  * FailAllocCoreChannelMethod). Failures not using the i-th method are ignored. */
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(fail_alloc_core_channel, "Control testing for hardware core channel allocation failure");
@@ -275,6 +281,11 @@ NvBool nvkms_kapi_sysmem_semaphores(void)
     return kapi_sysmem_semaphores;
 }
 
+NvBool nvkms_pushbuf_wrap_no_yield(void)
+{
+    return READ_ONCE(pushbuf_wrap_no_yield);
+}
+
 NvBool nvkms_conceal_vrr_caps(void)
 {
     return conceal_vrr_caps;
diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-os-interface.h b/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-os-interface.h
index 3103e42e..3e3d8e96 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-os-interface.h
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-os-interface.h
@@ -135,6 +135,7 @@ NvBool nvkms_enable_overlay_layers(void);
 NvBool nvkms_debug_logging(void);
 NvBool nvkms_dp_sst_edid_recovery_fix(void);
 NvBool nvkms_kapi_sysmem_semaphores(void);
+NvBool nvkms_pushbuf_wrap_no_yield(void);
 void nvkms_extcon_report_hdmi(NvBool state);
 void nvkms_extcon_report_hdmi_audio(NvBool state);
 
diff --git a/src/nvidia-modeset/os-interface/include/nvidia-modeset-os-interface.h b/src/nvidia-modeset/os-interface/include/nvidia-modeset-os-interface.h
index 3103e42e..3e3d8e96 100644
--- a/src/nvidia-modeset/os-interface/include/nvidia-modeset-os-interface.h
+++ b/src/nvidia-modeset/os-interface/include/nvidia-modeset-os-interface.h
@@ -135,6 +135,7 @@ NvBool nvkms_enable_overlay_layers(void);
 NvBool nvkms_debug_logging(void);
 NvBool nvkms_dp_sst_edid_recovery_fix(void);
 NvBool nvkms_kapi_sysmem_semaphores(void);
+NvBool nvkms_pushbuf_wrap_no_yield(void);
 void nvkms_extcon_report_hdmi(NvBool state);
 void nvkms_extcon_report_hdmi_audio(NvBool state);
 
diff --git a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-dma.c b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-dma.c
index 75e2046c..3f4b4bf3 100644
--- a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-dma.c
+++ b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-dma.c
@@ -123,6 +123,18 @@ void nvEvoMakeRoom(NVEvoChannelPtr pChannel, NvU32 count)
                     push_buffer->buffer = push_buffer->base;
                     nvDmaKickoffEvo(pChannel);
                     putOffset = 0;
+
+                    /*
+                     * The space from the start of the push buffer up to GET
+                     * is free now; check it without yielding first.
+                     * fifo_free_count still holds the space left before
+                     * the end, so falling through would always yield,
+                     * once per lap of the push buffer, with the NVKMS lock
+                     * held. With PUT at 0, the next pass can't wrap again.
+                     */
+                    if (nvkms_pushbuf_wrap_no_yield()) {
+                        continue;
+                    }
                 }
                 else if (putOffset != push_buffer->put_offset) {
                     nvDmaKickoffEvo(pChannel);
